3. f4 { The Vienna Gambit: White attacks e5 to open the f-file and gain the centre. }
3... d5 { The principled reply: strike in the centre before White's pawns roll on. }
4. fxe5 Nxe4 5. Nf3 Be7 6. d4 O-O 7. Bd3 { Challenging the e4 knight; White's e5 pawn cramps Black. }
7... f5 8. exf6 Bxf6 9. O-O { The f-file is open for White's rook and Black's centre is under pressure. } *
